# NEAR-LABEL: name:            far_tbb_non_layout
# Analyzed FBB is %bb.2 (near), not layout-next trap %bb.1.
# LUI/ADDI are EOL (`{{$}}`); cond dests include the trailing comma so
# `%bb.1` cannot prefix-match `%bb.12`. LABEL-scoped so a later function
# cannot satisfy dest/polarity.
# NEAR: bb.0.entry
# NEAR: $r6 = LUI{{.*}}%bb.3{{$}}
# NEAR: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.3{{$}}
# Invert dest != layout-next trap %bb.1; must be analyzed FBB %bb.2.
# NEAR-NOT: {{BEQZ|BNEZ}}{{.*}} $r7, %bb.1,
# NEAR: BNEZ{{.*}} $r7, %bb.2,
# Original BEQZ polarity must not remain; no leftover short B beside JALR.
# NEAR-NOT: BEQZ{{.*}} $r7
# NEAR-NOT: B %bb.
# NEAR: JALR
# NEAR-NOT: B %bb.
# NEAR: bb.1.trap
#
# FBB-LABEL: name:            far_fbb
# Original near cond to TBB survives; only trailing uncond is long-form.
# FBB: bb.0.entry
# FBB: $r6 = LUI{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# FBB: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# Original BEQZ polarity on in-range TBB; not inverted BNEZ.
# FBB-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}} $r7
# FBB: BEQZ{{.*}} $r7, %bb.1,
# FBB-NOT: BNEZ
# FBB-NOT: B %bb.
# FBB: JALR
# FBB-NOT: B %bb.
# FBB: bb.1.near
#
# MULTI-LABEL: name:            multi_control
# Unanalyzable two-cond tail whose last cycle is BUNDLE{ALU,B}: preceding
# BEQZs and the ALU sibling survive; only the selected uncond is replaced.
# Splice puts the coissued ALU before the first control; LUI+ADDI then
# land before that control; JALR is last. CHECK-NOT leftover B both after
# ADD32 (coissue member) and after the retained BEQZs.
# MULTI: bb.0.entry
# Coissued sibling (not any ADD32). Finalize may bake ADD32_E2_*.
# MULTI: $r3 = ADD32{{.*}} $r1, $r2
# MULTI-NOT: B %bb.
# MULTI: LUI{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# MULTI: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# MULTI: BEQZ{{.*}} $r4, %bb.1,
# MULTI: BEQZ{{.*}} $r5, %bb.1,
# MULTI-NOT: B %bb.
# MULTI: JALR
# MULTI-NOT: B %bb.
# MULTI: bb.1.near
